  "interpretation": [
    "The public layer/module learning-rate prior consistently moves code-change geometry closer to released Bonsai geometry and substantially improves depth-profile correlation.",
    "For binary recovery, the public prior also improves teacher KL on average for both exact-hard and categorical surrogates. Binary categorical-public has the lowest aggregate KL, while binary hard-public is the closest tested code geometry.",
    "For ternary recovery, the public prior improves geometry but modestly worsens aggregate KL; CAT-Q/auto remains the behavior winner and hard recovery remains closer to released code-change magnitude.",
    "All miniature runs under-shoot released code-change magnitude severely: about 7-8% versus 27-30% binary and 10-12% versus 36-42% ternary. The shape of the drift is already correct, especially by depth, but the recovery budget is too small to match final released geometry.",
    "The next method-selection experiment must vary recovery duration and learning-rate budget rather than further tuning only surrogate type."
